## [v1.3.0] - 2026-07-03

### Added
- **Inbound Stream Architecture**
  - Push-based inbound data ingestion via `POST /api/inbound/<stream_id>/data` with anti-enumeration responses, IP allowlist, coordinate validation, payload size limits, API key masking in logs, and per-stream rate limiting
  - `InboundStreamWorker` and `StreamManager` routing for push-based streams
  - Capture buffer and preview mode for inbound streams to inspect payloads before routing
  - Inbound stream UI integration with stream detail and configuration pages; Preview Mode badge rendered for inbound streams
  - Generic inbound plugins registered in plugin manager — display names updated for clarity:

    - `generic_inbound` → **JSON Receiver**
    - `generic_xml_inbound` → **XML Receiver**
    - `inbound_http` → **HTTP Location Endpoint**
    - `inbound_active` → **MQTT / WebSocket Client**

  - CA cert upload support for inbound streams
  - Inbound Receiver plugin for active-connect inbound sources

- **Active-Connect Inbound Plugins**
  - MQTT active-connect inbound plugin with TLS/mTLS support via existing cert infrastructure
  - WebSocket active-connect inbound plugin

- **UDP Multicast CoT Bridge**
  - `udp_multicast_listener` inbound plugin joins a UDP multicast group (default `239.2.3.1:6969`) and forwards received CoT to every TAK server on the stream — bridges LAN multicast across VPN/WAN links
  - Auto-detect wire format: CoT XML and TAK Protocol v1 Mesh SA protobuf (magic `0xbf 0x01 0xbf`) via `takproto`
  - IGMPv2 default with optional IGMPv3 source-specific multicast via `source_filter`
  - Configurable bind interface; per-source token-bucket rate limiting; first five dropped datagrams sampled into logs with source IP and hex preview
  - `bind_interface` now correctly binds to `INADDR_ANY` for multicast delivery while using the interface only for the IGMP join, fixing silent packet drops on specific-IP binds

- **CoT Forwarding Plugins** (category: `forwarding`)
  - `OutboundHTTP` plugin — POSTs or PUTs CoT events to an HTTP/HTTPS endpoint as JSON, raw XML, or custom template; scheme allow-listing prevents non-http/https URLs reaching network I/O
  - `OutboundMQTT` plugin — publishes CoT events to an MQTT broker with persistent paho connection, bounded queue with oldest-drop semantics, mqtts:// TLS via `cert_utils.build_ssl_context()`, and bad-auth detection
  - `OutboundWebSocket` plugin — persistent aiohttp WebSocket output with exponential backoff reconnect (cap 30s), background reader for proactive server-close detection, URL credential redaction in logs, and scheme allow-listing for ws/wss
  - `udp_multicast_publisher` — publishes CoT events to a UDP multicast group; forwarded event counts now persisted to the stream DB record via a batched flush every 30 seconds
  - Shared `services/output_plugin_helpers.py` — CoT extraction, formatting, geofence, dedup, rate-limit, and payload building extracted from legacy `webhook_handler` into a reusable module
  - Legacy `webhook_handler` plugin removed; documentation and dev guides updated to reference the three dedicated plugins

- **Notification Plugins** (category: `notification`)
  - `discord_handler`, `slack_handler`, `irc_handler` moved from the generic "Output" category to the dedicated **Notifications** display category; no behaviour changes

- **CoT Identity Heartbeat Improvements**
  - `how` attribute switched to `h-e` (human-entered) for team-member types so TAK Server accepts them
  - `precisionlocation` element added to team-member heartbeats for well-formed acceptance
  - `__group` always emitted with sensible team colour/role defaults
  - Identity CoT sent before queue drain on TX start so TAK Server sees TrakBridge before any event stream

- **Documentation**
  - `INBOUND_STREAMS_GUIDE.md` updated with UDP multicast plugin docs, wire format table, Docker networking guide (macvlan + `network_mode: host` topologies), and operator diagnostics
  - README updated with inbound stream support, UDP multicast bridge, and outbound HTTP/MQTT/WebSocket plugins in Features and Supported Providers sections

### Changed
- Dev container switched from Werkzeug reloader (`flask run --debug`) to Hypercorn, eliminating duplicate TAK connections and matching production topology
- `DevelopmentConfig.SQLALCHEMY_RECORD_QUERIES` now reads from `SQLALCHEMY_RECORD_QUERIES` env var (default `false`) instead of hardcoding `True`; production stays hardcoded `False`
- Werkzeug per-request access logs demoted to WARNING (reverse proxy already records them); `sqlalchemy.engine` dev override switched to WARNING with `SQLALCHEMY_RECORD_QUERIES` as the explicit opt-in
- CRLF header injection prevented at field level in `parse_custom_headers` for outbound HTTP plugin
- Mosquitto installed in all three integration-test CI jobs for outbound MQTT test coverage

### Fixed
- **Expired-password redirect** — Users with an expired password are now redirected to the change-password flow on login instead of being dropped into the application with an inconsistent state. Admins triggering a force-reset via the new `must_change_password` flag are likewise redirected on their next login
- **Admin password reset lockout** — Admin-initiated password resets no longer set `password_changed_at` to `None`, which previously caused the expiry check to treat the account as immediately expired and lock the user in a redirect loop. The new `must_change_password` boolean flag decouples forced-change from expiry state
- **`add_must_change_password` migration** — Fixed three defects introduced when the migration was originally merged: incorrect `down_revision` (`"add_inbound_stream_fields"` → `"54faa293e582"`); wrong table name (`"user"` → `"users"`) in both `upgrade()` and `downgrade()`; missing column name argument in `safe_add_column()` call
- **False-positive unhealthy warnings for output plugin workers** — Stream manager health checks no longer emit WARNING-level logs for output plugin workers (Discord, Slack, IRC, HTTP, MQTT, WebSocket, UDP multicast) that are operating normally; these workers lack a persistent TAK connection by design and are now recognised as healthy without one
- **TAK output worker task leak on stream save** — `_enhanced_transmission_worker` now cancels and awaits child `_tx_loop`/`_rx_worker` tasks in both `CancelledError` and `Exception` handlers, preventing orphaned tasks from spamming `Queue N does not exist` errors and tripping the circuit breaker on the freshly started worker
- **New worker connection closed on stream save** — `stop_worker` finally block now captures the connection as a local at the top of each iteration and only closes that specific connection, leaving a newer worker's registration intact
- **Stale worker entries never reaped** — `stop_stream` removes the worker in a `finally` block; `_periodic_health_check` now cross-references the DB and reaps workers for gone/inactive streams (INFO) instead of warning indefinitely
- **StreamWriter not closed on stop** — `stop_worker` now explicitly awaits `_cleanup_connection` (writer close + `wait_closed()`) before returning, sending TCP FIN to TAK Server synchronously
- **Migration column name missing** — `add_inbound_stream_fields` migration now passes column name as first positional arg to `sa.Column()`, unblocking the migration chain and downstream `ca_cert` column
- **Entrypoint `validate_schema` silent no-op** — bash `return validate_schema_optimized` returned the function name as a string; fixed to call the function and return its exit code
- **Entrypoint SIGTERM trap unreachable** — removed dead trap after `exec hypercorn`; Hypercorn as PID 1 handles signals directly
- **Entrypoint ANSI codes in Docker logs** — colour codes now gated on `[[ -t 2 ]]` so captured log output is plain text
- `identity CoT 'how'` test assertion updated to match `h-e` implementation
- HMAC `compare_digest` test updated to pass bytes (matching implementation)
- `inbound_stream` fixture uses `generic_xml_inbound` (a real registered plugin) so detail page renders Preview badge
- Mosquitto CI fixture: deduplicated `allow_anonymous` directive and surfaced stderr on startup failure; passwd file permissions relaxed to 0644 / temp dir 0755 for CI compatibility
- Identity CoT generation log demoted to DEBUG (was INFO, duplicated the TX send-site line)
- `outbound_websocket` `task_done()` now fires on every `queue.get()` including the re-enqueue path; `get_nowait()` drop-oldest branch also calls `task_done()`
- `OutboundWebSocket` and `OutboundHTTP` strip credentials from endpoint URL before logging

## [v1.2.3] - 2026-03-23

### Fixed
- TX worker now automatically reconnects with exponential backoff (5s→120s) when TAK server connectivity is lost and restored
- Circuit breaker resets before each reconnection attempt to prevent stale OPEN state from blocking recovery
- Circuit breaker now resets when a stream worker is stopped, preventing permanent connection loss after stream edits
- Circuit breaker resets during dead worker cleanup in start_worker() as a safety net
- Stale connection references cleaned up during worker stop to prevent dead socket reuse

## [v1.2.2] - 2026-03-21

### Added
- **Plugin-Overridable Minimum Poll Interval**
  - New `min_poll_interval` metadata key allows plugins to set poll floors as low as 1 seconds
  - Stream create/edit forms dynamically adjust minimum based on plugin metadata
  - JSON validator global floor lowered from 30 to 1 seconds
  - Backward compatible: plugins without the key default to 30-second minimum
  - Plugin Development Guide (wiki and docs) updated with usage examples

### Changed
- Queue max_size increased from 500 to 600 events for high-volume streams (e.g. AIS)
- Queue warning_threshold raised to 600 to match new capacity

### Fixed

- TX loop now breaks immediately on connection errors instead of retrying on a dead socket after stream config changes
- Identity heartbeat connection errors propagate to exit the TX loop cleanly
- Transmit batch aborts remaining events on connection loss instead of logging errors for each one
- RX worker uses exponential backoff (1s→60s) on repeated errors instead of fixed 1-second retry
- RX worker gives up after 5 consecutive SSL errors with actionable log message
- RX worker error logs now include TAK server ID, attempt count, and next retry delay
- Queue manager now reads max_size, queue_warning_threshold, and transmission settings from performance.yaml instead of using stale hardcoded defaults
- Hardcoded queue defaults updated from 500/400 to 600/600 to match performance.yaml

