  - SPOT plugin battery state mapping (GOOD→100, LOW→20) for accurate battery reporting
  - Default battery value of 100 when no battery data available
  - Case-insensitive battery state string handling
  - Battery state extraction from additional_data in CoT generation pipeline
  - Comprehensive battery testing across plugin and CoT integration layers

- **Garmin InReach Velocity and Course Extraction**
  - Parse velocity from Garmin KML ExtendedData format ("32.6 km/h") with automatic unit conversion to m/s
  - Support for multiple velocity units: km/h, kph, mph, m/s with intelligent default handling
  - Parse course/heading from Garmin KML format ("315.00 ° True") with degree normalization (0-360 range)
  - Top-level speed and course field placement for proper CoT integration
  - Automatic inclusion in team member `<track>` element and `<remarks>` for standard CoT types

- **Traccar Plugin Speed and Course Enhancement**
  - Moved speed and course from additional_data to top-level fields for CoT processing
  - Consistent data flow pattern matching Garmin implementation
  - None checking to prevent invalid data from being added
  - Proper handling of zero values (stationary devices)

- **Custom CoT XML Attributes System**
  - Plugin-extensible system for adding custom XML elements and attributes to CoT messages
  - Support for military symbols (`<__milsym>`), custom icons (`<usericon><iconsetpath/>`), link elements, and arbitrary XML
  - Protected element system preventing override of critical CoT structure (contact, uid, __group, status, track)
  - XML injection prevention with regex validation of element names
  - Special keys: `_text` for element text content, `_attributes` for XML attributes
  - Nested element support with flexible dict-based configuration
  - Event-level and detail-level attribute application
  - Simple string value support for element text content
  - Backward compatible - existing plugins work unchanged without custom attributes

### Changed
- **COT Generation Pipeline Enhancement**
  - Enhanced _create_pytak_events method to detect team member metadata in location additional_data
  - Modified _generate_cot_xml to generate appropriate XML structure for team members
  - Reuses existing COT pipeline completely with minimal code changes for maximum efficiency

### Technical Implementation
- **TDD Approach**: Complete test-driven development with comprehensive test coverage
- **Code Reuse**: Leverages existing COT pipeline, callsign mapping infrastructure, and UI patterns
- **Data Flow**: Configuration → Plugin Processing → COT Generation → Transmission (no changes to queuing or workers)
- **Compatibility**: Existing callsign mappings continue working unchanged (cot_type_override defaults to null)
- **Performance**: No additional database queries - team member data loaded with existing callsign mappings

